  "historical": {
    "title": "Why the completed metformin charge was higher",
    "body": "The completed charges are established by two paid pharmacy claims for metformin 500 mg tablets, quantity 60 for a 30-day supply. On August 18, 2026, Oak Street Pharmacy applied the preferred retail cost-share category and the member paid $8.00. On September 16, 2026, Lakeview Pharmacy applied the standard retail cost-share category and the member paid $27.00.\n\nThe pharmacy classifications match those categories: Oak Street Pharmacy was preferred retail on August 18, and Lakeview Pharmacy was standard retail on September 16. Under the selected policy for this plan and period, the matched 30-day metformin 500 mg supply is $8 at preferred retail and $27 at standard retail under the recorded conditions.",
